  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Cold front will continue to push offshore early\nthis morning, with high pressure building in from the west\nthrough most of this week. Temps will gradually warm through the\nweek as heights build. By mid to late week highs will again be\nback into the 80s for most of the area. A backdoor front may\nimpact the area Thu, but at this time just looks to be a wind\nshift. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...A stronger cold front will push through the area\nFriday night, with strong high pressure building in for the weekend.\nFront looks moisture starved, but could bring sct shower \nchances. Cooler and drier airmass will build into the region \nthis weekend, feeling like fall, with highs mainly in the 60s\nand lows in the 40s/50s. N-NW winds continue to trend a bit \nstronger behind the front, which could bring dangerous marine \nconditions along with the potential for coastal impacts. Though \ntoo soon for any specifics.",
